# GPU heap 0 through in-game 3D rebuilds at 3324x2494, the largest 4:3 picture DM_SCR_MAX_PX allows and the tightest shape (LIF-4, SHD-1): the Frame Drops controller is made to step the 3D scale down level by level
# and back up (DM_3D_SCALE_DYN_INJECT: every frame of the window counts as a drop; while it is set, Keep does not stop the controller, hle_oe.c), so
# every level's 3D colour and depth targets are rebuilt in game through the game's own rebuild call, the way Frame Drops does for a player.
# DM_3D_SCALE_FLOOR=0.6 lets it go deeper than the player's three levels below 100% (0.86 / 0.80 / 0.75): 1.00 -> 0.60 and back to 1.00, six
# rebuilds each way, the last one the largest (the 100% targets coming back into a heap the smaller ones used: +118 MiB in one step). The window (+0-4800, counted from the
# first judged frame) covers the six steps down; each step back up needs 15 clean windows (about 33 s). SMAA, Ultra and environment shadows, the
# interface path for screens narrower than 16:9 (DM_UI_169=1 DM_UI_YPOS=bottom). Measured 2026-11-03: down to 396 MiB used and back to 689 with
# a 76 MiB gap, the boot's own peak (16:9 4K: 683 and 84). It departs from this Mac's Recommended because only DM_GAME_RES renders this size here; heap
# readings are measurements, so it runs in front and in real full screen (the controller judges the real presents). Run it alone (about 5 minutes).
name s3d_cycle_3324x2494
requires cli
front fullscreen
save warlock
timeout 900
env DM_GAME_RES=3324x2494 DM_UI_169=1 DM_UI_YPOS=bottom DM_3D_SCALE=1.0 DM_3D_SCALE_DYN_INJECT=+0-4800 DM_3D_SCALE_FLOOR=0.6 DM_SHADOW_SIZE=4096 DM_ENV_SHADOWS=1 DM_AA_MODE=2 DM_TEST_FULLSCREEN_AT=1

expect main_menu timeout=150
enter_game
expect scale3d pct=60 timeout=400
expect scale3d pct=100 timeout=700
sleep 3
quit
check no_red
check no_red_log
check event scale3d pct=86
check event gpuheap pool_mb=768
